IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei6-part-9-coming-into-force`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-ii-table`
IMPORT `ei6-schedule-ii`

-- Tests of Schedule II (src:3247-3426): the interim provisions. Expected values are read from the text by hand.
-- Schedule II applies from June 30, 1996 until the provision it replaces comes into force: section 4 on January 1, 1997 and
-- sections 7, 14 and the others on January 5, 1997 (s 190(2), (3), (4); src:3173-3195).

§ `Paragraph 18 - the interim Schedule I`

-- Row 12 weeks (src:3386): eight blank cells, then 26, 28, 30, 32.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 12 (13.5%) EQUALS JUST 26
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 12 (20%) EQUALS JUST 32
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 12 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Row 13 weeks (src:3387): 24 in the eighth column.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 13 (12.5%) EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 13 (11.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Rows 20 and 21 (src:3394-3395): 14, 16, ... 36. Row 22 (src:3396): 15, 17, ... 37.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 20 (5%) EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 20 (20%) EQUALS JUST 36
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 21 (5%) EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 22 (5%) EQUALS JUST 15
-- Row 40 (src:3414): 24, 26, ... 44, 45. Row 41 (src:3415): 25, 27, ... 43, 45, 45.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 40 (5%) EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 40 (15.5%) EQUALS JUST 44
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 40 (16.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 41 (5%) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 41 (15.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
-- Row 52 (src:3426): 36, 38, 40, 42, 44, 45, ...
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 52 (5%) EQUALS JUST 36
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 52 (9.5%) EQUALS JUST 44
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 52 (10.5%) EQUALS JUST 45
-- No row for fewer than 12 weeks, more than 52, or a part of a week (fork F-ei6-8).
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 11 (20%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 53 (20%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 the maximum number of weeks of benefit` 12.5 (20%) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph 18 applies in place of Schedule I until January 5, 1997.
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 18 applies in place of Schedule I on the day` (YMD 1996 6 29))
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 applies in place of Schedule I on the day` (YMD 1996 6 30)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 18 applies in place of Schedule I on the day` (YMD 1997 1 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 18 applies in place of Schedule I on the day` (YMD 1997 1 5))

§ `Paragraphs 1 and 3 - section 4 and the definitions of attachment claimants`

#ASSERT `Schedule II para 1 s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 9 1) EQUALS JUST 39000
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 1 s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 12 31) EQUALS JUST 39000
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 1 s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings` (YMD 1997 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 1 s 4(1) the maximum yearly insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 6 29) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 1 s 4(2) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 9 1) EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 1 s 4(2) the maximum weekly insurable earnings` (YMD 1997 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 20 or more weeks: major; fewer than 20: minor (src:3264-3265); the definitions come into force on January 5, 1997.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 3 major attachment claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE 20
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 3 major attachment claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE 19)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 3 major attachment claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 3 major attachment claimant` (YMD 1997 1 5) TRUE 30)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 3 minor attachment claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE 19
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 3 minor attachment claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 3 minor attachment claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 3 minor attachment claimant` (YMD 1997 1 5) TRUE 10)

§ `Paragraph 4 - section 7`

#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(1) unemployment benefits are payable to the insured person` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(1) unemployment benefits are payable to the insured person` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(1) unemployment benefits are payable to the insured person` (YMD 1997 1 5) TRUE TRUE)
-- The table (src:3275-3283): 6% and under 20; 6-7 19; 7-8 18; 8-9 17; 9-10 16; 10-11 15; 11-12 14; 12-13 13; more than 13% 12.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (5%) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (6%) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (6.01%) EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (7%) EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (8%) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (9%) EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (10%) EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (11%) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (12%) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (13%) EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (13.01%) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) the required number of weeks of insurable employment` (20%) EQUALS 12
-- Qualification. Arguments: the day; a new entrant or re-entrant; an interruption of earnings; weeks; the rate (src:3270-3287).
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE TRUE 20 (5%)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE TRUE 19 (5%))
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE TRUE 19 (6.5%)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE TRUE 12 (14%)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE TRUE 11 (14%))
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE TRUE 26 (14%)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE TRUE 25 (14%))
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE FALSE 30 (5%))
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(2) and (3) the insured person qualifies to receive benefits` (YMD 1997 1 5) FALSE TRUE 30 (5%))
-- A new entrant or re-entrant: fewer than 14 weeks in all of the three kinds, no week counted twice (src:3289-3295; fork F-ei6-15).
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(4) the insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` (YMD 1996 10 1) 13 0 0
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(4) the insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` (YMD 1996 10 1) 14 0 0)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(4) the insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` (YMD 1996 10 1) 5 5 3
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(4) the insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` (YMD 1996 10 1) 5 5 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(4) the insured person is a new entrant or a re-entrant to the labour force` (YMD 1997 1 5) 0 0 0)
-- (6): the Canada-United States agreement.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 4 s 7(6) the claimant is not qualified to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 4 s 7(6) the claimant is not qualified to receive benefits` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE)

§ `Paragraph 5 - subsection 12(2)`

#ASSERT `Schedule II para 5 s 12(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period` (YMD 1996 10 1) 20 (5%) EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 5 s 12(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period` (YMD 1996 10 1) 12 (20%) EQUALS JUST 32
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 5 s 12(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period` (YMD 1996 10 1) 12 (12.5%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 5 s 12(2) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period` (YMD 1997 1 5) 20 (5%) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 6 - section 14`

-- It applies until section 14 comes into force on January 5, 1997, and after that for a benefit period that began before
-- January 5, 1997 (s 190(4), (5)).
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 applies in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` (YMD 1997 1 4) (YMD 1997 1 4)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 applies in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` (YMD 1997 3 1) (YMD 1996 12 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 6 applies in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` (YMD 1997 3 1) (YMD 1997 1 5))
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 6 applies in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` (YMD 1996 6 29) (YMD 1996 6 29))
-- (1): 55% of the average weekly insurable earnings, to a maximum of $413; with dependants 60% up to half of $750.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 500 FALSE EQUALS JUST 275
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 749 FALSE EQUALS JUST 412
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 750 FALSE EQUALS JUST 413
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 800 FALSE EQUALS JUST 413
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 375 TRUE EQUALS JUST 225
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 300 TRUE EQUALS JUST 180
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 376 TRUE EQUALS JUST 225
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 500 TRUE EQUALS JUST 275
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` TRUE 760 TRUE EQUALS JUST 413
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(1) the rate of weekly benefits` FALSE 500 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) and (3): the average weekly insurable earnings.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(2) the average weekly insurable earnings of a major attachment claimant` TRUE 10000 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(2) the average weekly insurable earnings of a major attachment claimant` FALSE 10000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The divisor table (src:3316-3322): not more than 8% 20; 8-9 19; 9-10 18; 10-11 17; 11-12 16; 12-13 15; more than 13% 14.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (5%) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (8%) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (8.01%) EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (9%) EQUALS 19
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (10%) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (11%) EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (12%) EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (13%) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the divisor for the regional rate of unemployment` (13.01%) EQUALS 14
-- The larger of the weeks and the divisor: 18 weeks at 5% (divisor 20) divides by 20; 22 weeks by 22; 15 weeks at 14% by 15.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant` TRUE 6000 18 (5%) EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant` TRUE 6600 22 (5%) EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant` TRUE 6000 15 (14%) EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant` TRUE 6000 12 (14%) EQUALS JUST (6000 DIVIDED BY 14)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 6 s 14(3) the average weekly insurable earnings of a minor attachment claimant` FALSE 6000 15 (14%) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Paragraphs 7 to 11`

-- 7: 25% of the weekly rate of benefit; only the excess is deducted.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 7 s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the week` (YMD 1996 10 1) 200 400 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 7 s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the week` (YMD 1996 10 1) 101 400 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 7 s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the week` (YMD 1996 10 1) 100 400 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 7 s 19(2) the amount deducted from the benefits payable for the week` (YMD 1997 1 5) 200 400 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 8: 20 or more weeks of insurable employment since the event.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 8 s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward against the claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) 20
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 8 s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward against the claimant` (YMD 1996 10 1) 19)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 8 s 28(4) no weeks of disqualification are carried forward against the claimant` (YMD 1997 1 5) 30)
-- 9: weeks since losing or leaving at least the number required by section 7; the restrictions.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 9(1) s 30(1)(a) the claimant has been employed in insurable employment for the number of weeks required by section 7` (YMD 1996 10 1) 20 20
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 9(1) s 30(1)(a) the claimant has been employed in insurable employment for the number of weeks required by section 7` (YMD 1996 10 1) 19 20)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 9(1) s 30(1)(a) the claimant has been employed in insurable employment for the number of weeks required by section 7` (YMD 1997 1 5) 30 20)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(5) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 7(2) or (3)` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(5) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 7(2) or (3)` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(5) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 7(2) or (3)` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(6) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 12(2) or section 14` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 9(2) s 30(6) the weeks may not be used for the purposes of subsection 12(2) or section 14` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE)
-- 10, 11: weeks accumulated with another employer after the suspension (or leave) at least those required by section 7.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 10 s 31(c) the claimant has accumulated with another employer the weeks required under section 7` (YMD 1996 10 1) 20 20
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 10 s 31(c) the claimant has accumulated with another employer the weeks required under section 7` (YMD 1996 10 1) 19 20)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 11 s 32(2)(c) the claimant has accumulated with another employer the weeks required under section 7` (YMD 1996 10 1) 14 14
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 11 s 32(2)(c) the claimant has accumulated with another employer the weeks required under section 7` (YMD 1996 10 1) 13 14)

§ `Paragraphs 12 to 15 - premiums`

#ASSERT `Schedule II para 12 s 66 the premium rate for 1996` (YMD 1996 12 31) (3%) EQUALS JUST (3%)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 12 s 66 the premium rate for 1996` (YMD 1997 1 1) (3%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 13 s 67(1) the employee's premium for the week` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE 1000 (3%) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 13 s 67(1) the employee's premium for the week` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE 1000 (3%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 13 s 67(1) the employee's premium for the week` (YMD 1997 1 1) TRUE 1000 (3%) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 13 s 67(2) the employer's premium for the week` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE 1000 (4.2%) EQUALS JUST 42
-- (3): earnings paid in a year after the year of the employment are deemed to belong to the year paid.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 13 s 67(3) the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` (YMD 1996 10 1) 1996 1997 EQUALS JUST 1997
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 13 s 67(3) the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` (YMD 1996 10 1) 1996 1996 EQUALS JUST 1996
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 13 s 67(3) the year in which the insurable employment is deemed to have occurred` (YMD 1996 10 1) 1996 1995 EQUALS JUST 1996
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 14 s 82(1) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration and remit it` (YMD 1996 10 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 14 s 82(1) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration and remit it` (YMD 1996 10 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Schedule II para 14 s 82(1) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration and remit it` (YMD 1997 1 5) TRUE)
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 14 s 82(1)(b) the amount to be remitted to the Receiver General` 30 42 EQUALS 72
-- 15: the excess of the deductions over the fixed percentage of the maximum yearly insurable earnings.
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 15 s 95 the overpayment made by the person` (YMD 1996 12 31) 1200 (3%) 39000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 15 s 95 the overpayment made by the person` (YMD 1996 12 31) 1170 (3%) 39000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 15 s 95 the overpayment made by the person` (YMD 1996 12 31) 1200 (3%) 39000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Schedule II para 15 s 95 the overpayment made by the person` (YMD 1997 1 1) 1200 (3%) 39000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

